1
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:19,470
'The play may begin at any moment,' I said.

2
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:24,550
'It may have begun already,' Susan answered.

3
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:27,780
I hurried to the ticket office.

4
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:31,436
'May I have two tickets please?'

5
00:00:31,436 --> 00:00:32,350
I asked.

6
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:37,100
'I'm sorry, we've sold out,' the girl said.

7
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,826
'What a pity!'

8
00:00:38,826 --> 00:00:41,510
Susan exclaimed.

9
00:00:41,510 --> 00:00:46,590
Just then, a man hurried to the ticket office.

10
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:50,152
'Can I return these two tickets?'

11
00:00:50,152 --> 00:00:51,150
he asked.

12
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:55,050
'Certainly,' the girl said.

13
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:59,440
I went back to the ticket office at once.

14
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:04,274
'Could I have those two tickets please?'

15
00:01:04,274 --> 00:01:05,210
I asked.

16
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:12,400
'Certainly,' the girl said, 'but they're for next Wednesday's performance.

17
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:15,350
Do you still want them?'

18
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:23,268
'I might as well have them,' I said sadly.
